    "body": "## Summary\n\nADR-033 Commit 1: CSS position support for **relative + fixed**. Absolute and sticky are parsed but treated as static in v1.\n\n## Zero-visible-delta, honestly predicted and verified\n\nThis ADR's spec predicted zero visible delta. The pre-commit check confirmed it:\n\n- PNG at viewport 1774 rendered byte-identical to pre-ADR-033 PNG\n- Measurement at implementation time: **14 relative elements (all no-op), 0 fixed elements in first viewport, 1 absolute element (search icon, deferred to ADR-034)**\n\nThe 3 `position:fixed` rules in Wikipedia's CSS target `.vector-page-titlebar-toc` (TOC toggle) — not in the first viewport. All 22 `position:relative` rules have zero actual `top`/`left`/`bottom`/`right` offsets (context-only).\n\n## What ships\n\n### Position enum + LayoutBox field\n\n```cpp\nenum class Position { Static, Relative, Absolute, Fixed, Sticky };\nLayoutBox::position = Position::Static;  // default\n```\n\nSet during `layout_element` from `ComputedStyle::get(\"position\")`.\n\n### position: fixed - out-of-flow + viewport anchor\n\n- Skipped from parent's block flow (parent `cursor_y` doesn't advance; parent height excludes fixed child)\n- Positioned at `(top, left)` offsets from ComputedStyle, viewport coordinates\n- `top: auto` / `left: auto` → `0` (v1)\n- v1: `top` / `left` only (all 3 Wikipedia fixed rules use `top:12px; left:12px`)\n- v1: no scroll interaction (anchored to initial viewport top-left)\n\n### position: relative - no-op + context prep\n\nStored on `LayoutBox`, no layout change. Future absolute children can use it as their containing block in ADR-034.\n\n### absolute / sticky - parsed, treated as static\n\nStore the enum value for future ADRs. Layout as `static` in v1. The search icon (`span.cdx-text-input__icon` with `top=50% left=9px`) renders in-flow at approximately correct position by accident; correct positioning requires containing-block tracking (ADR-034).\n\n## What this prepares for\n\n**ADR-034 (`position: absolute`)**: the search icon gets proper containing-block anchoring. That's where the first real visible delta from the position arc lands.\n\n**z-index**: needs `position` to establish stacking contexts.\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before ADR-033 Commit 1: 414 / 1710\n- After: **421 / 1737** (+7 / +27)\n- Full suite all pass, zero warnings\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `position: relative` stored on LayoutBox | ✅ |\n| `position: static` default | ✅ |\n| `position: fixed` anchored at `(top, left)` | ✅ |\n| `position: fixed` without offsets at `(0, 0)` | ✅ |\n| `position: fixed` skipped from parent flow | ✅ |\n| `position: absolute` stored, treated as static | ✅ |\n| `position: relative` offsets ignored (v1) | ✅ |\n| **PNG byte-identical to pre-ADR-033** | ✅ (zero visible delta, as predicted) |\n| No regression to prior ADRs | ✅ |\n| Full suite green | ✅ |\n\n## Honest note\n\nThe commit message says it plainly: **this ADR produces zero visible delta**. Its value is structural — position infrastructure for ADR-034 (absolute + containing blocks) and future z-index.\n\nSame discipline as ADR-032: ship the structural piece, document the honest zero/negative result, let the next ADR build on the foundation.\n\nRefs #174\n",
